frontage-chart vendors uPlot (https://github.com/leeoniya/uPlot), copyright
Leon Sorokin, under the MIT License, at
frontage-chart/frontage_chart/_browser/uplot.js. It is vendored rather than
fetched so that a build needs no network and an app has no CDN in its
critical path; its licence travels in the file's own header.

frontage-map vendors Leaflet (https://leafletjs.com), copyright Vladimir
Agafonkin and CloudMade, under the BSD 2-Clause License, at
frontage-map/frontage_map/_browser/leaflet.js and, as the first part of
index.css, leaflet.css. Both are verbatim except for four added lines in the
JavaScript — a CommonJS shim and an `export default`, marked in the file — and
two appended CSS rules, marked likewise. Vendored rather than fetched for the
same reason as uPlot; its licence travels in the file's own header.

Map *tiles* are not vendored and cannot be: a basemap is fetched at runtime
from whatever tile server the app names. The default is OpenStreetMap's, whose
tile usage policy applies to any app that ships with it
(https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/). `tiles=None` requests
no tiles at all.

frontage-layout and frontage-table contain no third-party code.
